  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Season chicken with salt & pepper. Heat olive oil over medium heat and cook chicken until no pink remains. Set aside."
    },
    {
      "text": "Add onion and garlic to the pan. Cook until onion is tender, about 3 minutes."
    },
    {
      "text": "Add 3 cups broth, tomatoes, cream, parsley, and Italian seasoning and bring to a boil. Add pasta. Let simmer for about 15 minutes or until tender and thickened. If you need, add ½ cup broth till pasta is cooked. Mix in ¼ cup parmesan cheese."
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the chicken back to skillet, top with mozzarella cheese and remaining ¼ cup parmesan, then broil 2-3 minutes or until cheese is melted and golden."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "NotesKeep leftovers in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 4 days, and in the freezer for up to 2 months.",
